  <h2>What a technical director does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Write the technical specifications from the intent of the project.</li>
    <li>Make the calls: technical choices, suppliers, technical budget and cost tracking.</li>
    <li>Have the drawings produced and approve them: site layout, schematics, rigging.</li>
    <li>Coordinate structural studies with an engineering office.</li>
    <li>Manage the suppliers during load-in, the show period and the strike.</li>
    <li>Be the technical point of contact for the venue, the production and the authorities.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Technical director, production manager, stage manager</h2>
  <p>These three roles complement each other. The <strong>technical director</strong> designs the set-up and makes the calls. The <strong>production manager</strong> keeps the site running: schedule, access, co-activity, crews and suppliers. The <strong>stage manager</strong> runs the stage during the show: running orders, entrances, changeovers and timing. On a small event, one person can cover several roles; on a stadium production, each has their own team.</p>

  <h2>When to bring one in</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>At the start of the project, before consulting suppliers: that is when feasibility and budget are decided.</li>
    <li>When there are many suppliers and nobody is holding the whole thing together.</li>
    <li>When the venue is not designed to host the format (stadium, monument, outdoor site).</li>
    <li>For a venue or organisation that produces all year round and wants a single technical point of contact.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>For how long?</h2>
  <p>From a few days of support on a specific phase to full technical direction, from design to handing the venue back. At ESE, four formats: day-rate support, targeted mission, full production, year-round support.</p>

  <h2>What ESE does</h2>
  <p>ESE provides technical direction for events of all sizes, from the Paris 2024 Games ceremonies (compliance, safety and fire prevention, alongside Paname 24) to the Pope's visit to the Stade de France, as well as concerts at the Accor Arena and brand events.</p>
